# Deploys run from the REPO ROOT (the Vercel project's Root Directory is "frontend"),
# and the uploader applies only this file / the root .gitignore -- nested .gitignore
# files are not consulted. frontend/.gitignore's "dist" rule therefore does not apply
# to the upload, and a previous local build used to be shipped into the build context.
#
# That was not cosmetic. Tailwind v4 auto-detects its sources by walking the project,
# so it scanned the last bundle and harvested class-like tokens out of it -- emitting
# 14 utilities nothing uses plus their !important variants, +2.5kB, and leaving
# production CSS unreproducible from a clean checkout. Keep build output out of here.
frontend/dist
frontend/node_modules
frontend/coverage

# The .NET half of the repo is irrelevant to the frontend build and is the larger part
# of the upload.
src
tests
AltitudELog.slnx
Directory.Build.props
Dockerfile
docker-compose.yml
